    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a publicly traded enterprise software company, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, California, that provides cloud-based applications for human resources, finance, and IT. The company trades on the public markets under the ticker WDAY and reported revenue of approximately $9.552 billion for the fiscal year ending January 31, 2026, according to its most recent 10-K filing.\n\nWorkday describes its core offering as an enterprise AI platform and positions its primary AI product, Workday AI, around HR and finance workflows, skills-based talent management, and predictive analytics. The company's website promotes what it calls agentic AI, described as specialized agents capable of finding, building, acting, and automating processes across HR, finance, and IT, including a capability referenced in connection with a product called Sana. The held facts categorize Workday AI under ERP and business application AI, with a noted concern around sensitive HR data exposure.\n\nWorkday faces a notable volume of federal litigation. Cases on record include multiple actions brought by Meckfessel Poletti in the Eastern District of California, Williams v. Workday in the Northern District of Georgia, Elias v. Workday in the Northern District of California, Noriega and Doe matters in the District of Colorado, and Hill v. Workday actions filed in both the District of Maryland and the Eastern District of Virginia.",
